From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: release the MLD-address entry with its STA-MLD
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

hostapd's assoclist names an MLO client by its MLD address, so the
polled refresh adds a stalist entry under that address next to the
per-leg entries the events create. On disconnect, stamld_clean()
releases the affiliated legs - and nothing else. The MLD-address entry
lives on, this node keeps listing the departed client in its Associated
Clients TLV, and the controller keeps handing the client back to the
node it already left.

Measured 2026-08-05: bpi-8g still claimed the client at 03:15, thirteen
minutes after its own hostapd deauthed it (03:02:40), and the
controller obediently flipped sta ownership back to bpi-8g while the
client was associated elsewhere.

Look the MLD-address entry up before freeing the STA-MLD and release it
through wifi_del_sta(), which also keeps num_sta and the assoc-control
bookkeeping straight.

--- a/src/agent_ubus_events.c
+++ b/src/agent_ubus_events.c
@@ -636,6 +636,22 @@
 		if (data[4] && hwaddr_aton(blobmsg_data(data[4]), mlo_macaddr)) {
 			stamld = agent_get_stamld(a, mlo_macaddr);
 			if (stamld) {
+				struct sta *mld_s = agent_get_sta(a, mlo_macaddr);
+
+				/* The polled assoclist registers the client under its
+				 * MLD address too, and stamld_clean() only releases the
+				 * affiliated legs. The MLD-address entry lived on, so
+				 * this node kept reporting a departed client in its
+				 * Associated Clients TLV, and the controller kept
+				 * handing the client back to it. Release it with the
+				 * STA-MLD. */
+				if (mld_s) {
+					struct netif_ap *mld_ap = agent_get_ap(a, mld_s->bssid);
+
+					if (mld_ap)
+						wifi_del_sta(a, mld_ap->ifname, mlo_macaddr);
+				}
+
 				stamld_free(a, stamld);
 				return;
 			}
